## Exact next split

### Full-core branch

Do not redo §§100--119 merely to enlarge a numerical window or re-prove the exact
floor endpoint exclusion. The live source-level target is now the interaction of
§§122--123 and the
\(\liminf\mu_D\ge1.6375621841815\ldots\) loaded-chord/train floor with the
global loaded-hull/diameter ledger.

Section 122 forces

\[
\sum_r(L_r+P_{{\rm exc},r}-2d_r)
\ge
\left[{\pi\over2}(2-\sqrt3)-o(1)\right]D,
\]

while Section 123 gives

\[
\sum_rP_{{\rm exc},r}\le10(e_{BB}-k).
\]

Therefore focus on the aggregate outer-walk detour

\[
\boxed{\sum_r(L_r-2d_r)}
\]

and its coupling to `e_BB-k` and the actual diameter graph.

Acceptable closing routes are:

1. prove an upper bound on the **same aggregate detour** strong enough to contradict §122 after paying `P_exc` with §123;
2. use global diameter minimality to turn the forced aggregate detour into a source-preserving strict decrease of the global diameter;
3. force an exact unit equilateral triangle directly from the loaded-hull / harmonic-cell geometry;
4. prove a genuinely boundary-order local filling theorem that closes the §§120--121 anisotropic moment bridge and then globalize it.

A limiting moment argument must control the Section-121 error at scale `o(d)`, not merely `o(D^2)`.

### Macroscopic inactive-container branch

One internal inactive chamber or exterior cap has quadratic population/area and only `O(D)` perimeter/slack. For an internal chamber, hull stability and deep matching give a protected isolate hull and isolate-only blocker graph. Proof-only §95 shows contact creation alone need not transfer positive KKT force.

The missing theorem must force an exact unit triangle, alter or replace part of the old diameter-carrying core, or construct a same-cardinality feasible source with strictly smaller global diameter.

## Binding dead routes

Do not use without a new proof:

- incident-diameter sequence `=>` Euler trail/path;
- FB4 force-bulk localization;
- incompatible-cut C53 pentagon objection;
- RSR disk-equality uniqueness;
- Eppstein near-equality `=>` near quadrangulation;
- five-host measure saturation `=>` all hosts occupied;
- inward OP pocket `subset` exterior Reuleaux minor cap;
- deletion of contact-isolated source points;
- full-source extension of the §57 affine-kernel theorem;
- `r/(6C_T)` as the sharp limit of the Section-90 bin method;
- `G_loc=o(D^2) => G_loc/d=o(1)` in Section 121.

## Research standard

Before promoting a new lemma, write its exact dependency chain to either an exact unit triangle, a source-preserving strict sub-`D` competitor, or the Level I conclusion. A computation may certify finite arithmetic or a regression; it does not supply global optimality.
